plugins.description:
Bring your Canva design workflow into Codex and create, refine, and review designs through natural conversation.

What Canva can do: 
Create designs: Turn a brief, outline, or draft copy into a presentation, doc, poster, flyer, social post, resume, and more. 
Generate images: Create photos, illustrations, icons, and graphics from a prompt, or restyle an image you already have. 
Remove backgrounds: Lift the subject out of an image onto a transparent background. Upload files: Bring attachments and files from your chat into Canva to use in your designs. 
Resize for social media: Adapt a design for Facebook, Instagram, and LinkedIn in one step. 
Bulk create: Generate multiple designs from spreadsheet data using a brand template. 
Edit designs: Update text, media, and formatting, or reposition and resize elements. 
Get design feedback: Receive structured feedback on visual hierarchy, layout, readability, consistency, and accessibility. 
Implement feedback: Review comment threads and apply clear, actionable changes. Brand check: Check colors, fonts, logo usage, and copy against your Brand Kit.

Once installed, describe what you want in plain language or invoke Canva directly with @Canva.

Try prompts like:

@Canva, create a pitch deck from this outline.
@Canva, make an Instagram post announcing our Friday sale.
@Canva, generate an illustration of a lighthouse at dawn.
@Canva, remove the background from this photo.
@Canva, upload this PDF and turn it into a presentation.
@Canva, resize this design for social media.
@Canva, create designs from this spreadsheet using my brand template.
@Canva, update the headline in this design.
@Canva, implement the feedback in the comment threads.
@Canva, check this design against my Brand Kit.
Requirements: Connect your Canva account to use the plugin. Bulk Create requires an eligible Canva Enterprise plan. Design and image generation use Canva AI credits.

Want to take a more hands-on approach? Instantly open your design in Canva's power

MindMap turns outlines into interactive, collapsible mind maps inside ChatGPT. Paste or describe a topic and MindFlow renders a visual map you can explore with pan/zoom and fullscreen. Click any node for an instant explanation so you can study, plan, onboard, or brainstorm faster.

@MindMap Visualise deep learning topics
@MindMap Visualise dog breeds
@MindMap Mindmap of biological tree of life

MonPIF connects ChatGPT to the official Fédération Wallonie-Bruxelles (Belgium) Common Core Curriculum framework. Every answer about learning objectives is retrieved directly from the official database — not invented, not paraphrased.

Designed for homeschooling families, MonPIF helps you:

- explore official learning objectives by subject and grade level;
- build a realistic annual learning plan;
- connect everyday activities to the learning objectives they cover;
- prepare your Individual Learning Plan (PIF) using official FWB texts.

Simply ask a question — MonPIF loads the curriculum framework and responds with the exact official wording.

You get educational guidance grounded in the official curriculum, without having to navigate the framework yourself.

Manage and search universal gift lists and registries without leaving ChatGPT. Conveniently discover and add gifts from any store, search registries and gift lists, and enjoy a seamless gifting experience. MyRegistry makes it easy for friends and family to get you the perfect gift. 
Once installed, describe what you want or invoke MyRegistry directly with @MyRegistry. Try prompts like:
@MyRegistry, does a friend of mine have a gift list?
@MyRegistry, add gifts to my gift list.
@MyRegistry, search for a friend's wedding registry.
@MyRegistry, show me gifts between $50-$100
@MyRegistry, find my friend's holiday gift list
@MyRegistry, does this organization have a giving list?
